# New screen build kickoff

User wants to build new consumer screen(s) in the `{{CONSUMER_FILE_NAME}}` file using {{SYSTEM_NAME}}
components and tokens.

## Required skill loads

Load all of these at session start:
- `skills/ds-tokens.md` — token reference
- `skills/ds-components.md` — component keys
- `skills/screens.md` — screen-building patterns and conventions
- `skills/figma-gotchas.md` — Plugin API traps (MANDATORY before any use_figma call)

## Standard build workflow

1. **Ask user** for:
   - Reference design (a Figma node ID in the reference file, or a description)
   - Target placement (which page + section + section-relative position)
   - Screen name convention (e.g., "Profile / Default")

2. **Inspect reference** via `get_design_context` if a Figma node is provided

3. **Plan in `yaml` block** before building:
   - Layout structure (content frame, chrome, sub-frames)
   - Component instances needed (with keys from `ds-components.md`)
   - Token bindings expected (with keys from `ds-tokens.md`)
   - Honest scope notes (any gaps in {{SYSTEM_NAME}} that need workarounds)

4. **Build incrementally** with render-verify between phases:
   - Phase 1: Screen frame + content shell
   - Phase 2: Main content (cards, forms, etc.)
   - Phase 3: Chrome (Status Bar, inner-screen top nav if applicable, Home Indicator)
   - Phase 4: Scroll pattern (numberOfFixedChildren, overflowDirection)
   - Phase 5: **Binding audit** — walk all NEW frames/text built outside of {{SYSTEM_NAME}} instances,
     confirm zero unbound elements (see `figma-gotchas.md`, the clone-drops-bindings trap)

5. **After each phase**: `figma_get_component_image` to verify

6. **Final audit**: walk the new screen, count bound fills/strokes/text styles, report
   - 0 hardcoded fills (excluding white/black for screen-page backgrounds and overlays)
   - 0 hardcoded strokes
   - 100% text nodes have textStyleId (or noted exception)
   - 0 unbound corner radii on cards/buttons/inputs
   - 0 unbound stroke weights on bordered elements

## Required conventions (per screens.md)

- Mobile frame: {{FRAME_W}}×{{FRAME_H}}
- Page background: `{{PAGE_BG_TOKEN}}`
- Prefer the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} component for every standard element — inner-screen headers, list/menu
  rows, hero amount fields, dialogs — never hand-build an equivalent. When {{SYSTEM_NAME}} is missing a
  variant, use the closest substitute and file a gap to the DS context.
- Chrome at END of children, `numberOfFixedChildren` counts from end
- `overflowDirection = "VERTICAL"` if scrollable, `"NONE"` otherwise

