## Critical gotchas to remember

(All numbered in `figma-gotchas.md` — load it first.)

- **Font loading mandatory** — load every {{FONTS}} weight before any text op
- **`swapComponent` resets vector fill bindings** — always re-bind after swap
- **`SECTION.appendChild` reinterprets coords as section-relative** — append first, then set x/y
- **`layoutSizingHorizontal` requires parent IS auto-layout + node already appended**
- **Anchor frame pattern** — when wrapping toggleable side slots around centered content, use fixed
  anchor frames so center stays centered regardless of toggle state
- **URL node-IDs may resolve to pages, not components** — when `figma_get_component` returns
  `type: "CANVAS"`, scan children for the real COMPONENT_SET
- **Variants outside component_set bounds break the variant picker** — if you clone a variant to extend
  a set, restack inside the parent bounds
- **Binding completeness must be audited, not assumed** — `clone()` does NOT preserve setBoundVariable
  references. Run the audit script from `figma-gotchas.md` on any new component or sub-frame before final
  delivery. Target zero unbound elements.

## Honest scope reminders

- Always offer to update the consumer file audit after building
- If a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap is hit (missing token, missing style, missing icon), flag honestly:
  - Use the closest substitute
  - Document the gap in scope notes
  - Suggest a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} update for the next publish cycle
- Track known unresolved gaps (missing text styles, missing tokens, no dedicated component for a need)
  and their agreed workarounds, so each build inherits the current list instead of rediscovering them.

## Communication style

- Skip apologies. Direct.
- `yaml` planning blocks before each phase.
- Render-verify visually after every phase — no "looks fine" without screenshot.
- Always include the binding audit as the final phase before delivery.
- End with a structured delivery summary listing what's done + scope notes + audit results (must show
  zero unbound elements).
